# Slide To Reveal — a blurred 6-digit code (112358) drawn in Skia; dragging a
# finger over it opens a blurred circular mask (alpha + luminance masks) that
# un-blurs and scales up the digits near the finger, fading back on release.
# What this test covers: a slow drag across every digit, a press-and-hold in
# place (mask fades in without movement), a vertical drag, a drag that leaves
# the canvas bounds (event.x/y outside the card), quick repeated taps
# (fade in/out interrupted), a fast zig-zag, and release/fade-out.
context platform=ios
open "demos://animations/slide-to-reveal"
wait "label=\"Close\"" 45000
# Warm-up touch on the status bar: the first touch of a test can be lost while
# the XCTest runner attaches.
press 330 20
wait 500
wait 1500
# Card spans x 80..321, y 397..477 (centre 201,437).
gesture pan 95 437 210 0 2500
wait 1000
longpress 201 437 1500
wait 1000
gesture pan 150 400 0 75 800
wait 800
# Start inside the card, leave it to the right and below.
gesture pan 250 437 140 200 1000
wait 1000
press 120 437 --count 5 --interval-ms 120
wait 800
gesture pan 90 420 220 40 300
gesture pan 310 460 -220 -40 300
gesture pan 90 437 220 0 200
wait 1500
wait "label=\"Close\"" 15000
press "role=\"button\" label=\"Close\""
wait 1500
